{"id":"NCT06902558","title":"ANCHOR Study: A Study to Assess the Safety and Efficacy of ABBV-CLS-628 in Adult Participants With Autosomal Dominant Polycystic Kidney Disease (ADPKD)","official":"A Phase 2, Multicenter, Randomized, Double-blind, Placebo-controlled Study to Evaluate the Safety and Efficacy of ABBV-CLS-628 in Adult Subjects With Autosomal Dominant Polycystic Kidney Disease (ADPKD)","summary":"Autosomal Dominant Polycystic Kidney Disease (ADPKD) is the most common genetic cause of kidney disease that causes fluid-filled cysts to develop in the kidneys. The purpose of this study is to assess the safety and efficacy of ABBV-CLS-628 for the treatment of ADPKD in adult participants.\n\nABBV-CLS-628 is an investigational drug being developed for the treatment of ADPKD. Participants are placed in 1 of 4 groups, called treatment arms. Each group receives a different treatment. There is a 1 in 4 chance that participants will be assigned to placebo. Around 240 adult participants with ADPKD will be enrolled at approximately 100 sites worldwide.\n\nParticipants will receive IntraVenous ABBV-CLS-628 or placebo every 4 weeks for 92 weeks. Participants will be followed for up to 15 weeks.\n\nThere may be higher treatment burden for participants in this trial compared to their standard of care . Participants will attend regular visits during the study at a hospital or clinic. The effect of the treatment will be checked by medical assessments, blood tests, checking for side effects and completing questionnaires.","conditions":["Autosomal Dominant Polycystic Kidney Disease"],"interventions":[{"type":"DRUG","name":"ABBV-CLS-628"},{"type":"DRUG","name":"Placebo"}],"criteria":"Inclusion Criteria:\n\n* Autosomal Dominant Polycystic Kidney Disease (ADPKD) Class 1C, 1D, or 1E based on the Mayo Clinic Imaging Classification of ADPKD.\n* Estimated glomerular filtration rate (eGFR) \\>= 30 mL/min/1.73 m\\^2 and \\< 90 mL/min/1.73 m\\^2, using the Chronic Kidney Disease Epidemiology Collaboration (CKD-EPI) equation at Screening.\n\nExclusion Criteria:\n\n* Current interventions to treat ADPKD such as non-approved medications or lifestyle modifications.\n* Any exclusionary medical diseases, disorders, or conditions as described in the protocol.","minAge":"18 Years","maxAge":"55 Years","sex":"ALL","healthy":false,"studyType":"INTERVENTIONAL","purpose":"TREATMENT","enrollment":240,"start":"2025-06-09","pcd":"2029-08","upd":"2026-10-06","sponsor":"Calico Life Sciences LLC","areas":["other"],"central":["Calico Clinical Trial Communication · 650-754-6200 · clinicaltrialcommunication@calicolabs.com"],"sites":[{"f":"University of Alabama at Birmingham","city":"Birmingham","pr":"Alabama","zip":"35294","s":"R","lat":33.5207,"lon":-86.8025,"c":"Maria El Hachem · 205-975-0549 · mehachem@uabmc.edu"},{"f":"Valiance Clinical Research - Huntington Park","city":"Huntington Park","pr":"California","zip":"90255","s":"R","lat":33.9817,"lon":-118.2251,"c":"Josh Lai · 323-484-0508 · j.lai@ValianceClinicalResearch.com"},{"f":"Academic Medical Research Institute (AMRI) - Los Angeles","city":"Los Angeles","pr":"California","zip":"90022","s":"R","lat":34.0522,"lon":-118.2437,"c":"Mohamed Shahawy, MD, MPH · 323-725-0051 · md@amrionline.net"},{"f":"UC Irvine Medical Center","city":"Orange","pr":"California","zip":"92868-3201","s":"R","lat":33.7878,"lon":-117.8531,"c":"Ahmad Walid Roshan · 714-509-6271 · ahmadwar@hs.uci.edu"},{"f":"National Institute of Clinical Research - Pomona","city":"Pomona","pr":"California","zip":"91768","s":"R","lat":34.0553,"lon":-117.7523,"c":"National Institute of Clinical Research, Inc. · 323-725-0657 · nicr@nicresearch.com"},{"f":"University Of California, San Francisco","city":"San Francisco","pr":"California","zip":"94143-2202","s":"R","lat":37.7749,"lon":-122.4194,"c":"Meyeon Park, MD · 415-514-1122 · PKD@ucsf.edu"},{"f":"University of California Los Angeles Medical Center","city":"Santa Monica","pr":"California","zip":"90404","s":"NYR",